{"title":"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 7","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems\">2009 AMC 10B #7</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_12B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 12B Problems\">2009 AMC 12B #6</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>By inserting parentheses, it is possible to give the expression\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/4/5749b941fd5ab876b3610ecff97cfbbf6ffd4981.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2\\times3 + 4\\times5\\]\" width=\"102\" height=\"14\" />\nseveral values.  How many different values can be obtained?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/4/ce4e305858d2968a7a35e72d8e8d6f848ef4e8a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{(A) } 2 \\qquad \\text{(B) } 3 \\qquad \\text{(C) } 4 \\qquad \\text{(D) } 5 \\qquad \\text{(E) } 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"330\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The three operations can be performed on any of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/b/4db3b59940e4f5cd42bbab2b7815c452a0197507.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3! = 6$\" width=\"47\" height=\"13\" /> orders.  However, if the addition is performed either first or last, then multiplying in either order produces the same result. So at most four distinct values can be obtained.  It is easy to check that the values of the four expressions\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/4/ae4e15557bcda228a1dbe886c24d7814e740971d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} (2\\times3) + (4\\times5) &amp;= 26,\\\\ (2\\times3 + 4)\\times5 &amp;= 50,\\\\ 2\\times(3 + 4\\times5) &amp;= 46,\\\\ 2\\times(3 + 4)\\times5 &amp;= 70 \\end{align*}\" width=\"176\" height=\"93\" />\nare in fact all distinct.  So the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4c6c07150a0f6e56b0a6e198d1d19155dfe96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"22\" height=\"25\" />, which is choice <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/8/2484f88154fadcf9c781bba19becdae88696b77f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(C)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"25\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We use constructive counting. From <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aaf4c9ecc010eb8d4fd4219205bc45b9091e44db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 3 + 4 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" /> there are four ways to place the \"(\". Then, there are four ways to place the \")\". That accounts for 16 plausible cases.\n</p><p><b>Lemma:</b> Each value is repeated four times each. We claim the answer is 4.\n</p><p><b>Proof of the Lemma:</b>\n</p><p>Very straightforward. For the single <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/f/05f0dbf57e54630047e1bd9aa30f6f8bfbf4b690.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2) \\times 3 + 4 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"119\" height=\"20\" /> obviously we see it is repeated four times. For the double, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/1/651f53520399a5938558640a93d7967941ed0c74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(2 \\times 3) + 4 \\times 5 = 2 \\times 3 + (4 \\times 5)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"260\" height=\"20\" /> is the same. A counting argument easily shows that if one places each of the parentheses such that it follows the Law of PEMDAS, then we obtain cases where we have a repeated sum. We handwave the rest of the proof as an interesting exercise for the reader, but the proof can be built upon PEMDAS.\n</p><p><b>2009 AMC 10B P7</b>\n</p><p>The answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/4/6c4c6c07150a0f6e56b0a6e198d1d19155dfe96c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"22\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_7&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B\">2009 AMC 10B</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 6\">Problem 6</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8\">Problem 8</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 AMC 10B Problems/P